# Skill: Testing

> **NUNCA entregar codigo sin tests. Cobertura < 80% = tarea INCOMPLETA.**

## Cobertura obligatoria

| Capa | Minimo |
|------|--------|
| Use Cases | 90% |
| Repos / Servicios / Controllers | 80% |
| **Global** | **80%** |

## Escenarios minimos

| Tipo | Escenarios |
|------|------------|
| Use Case | exitoso + error + input invalido |
| Repositorio | respuesta OK + error red/BD |
| Controller | 200 + 400/404 + error no controlado |

## Ubicacion

| Proyecto | Convencion | Ejemplo |
|----------|------------|---------|
| Frontend | `__tests__/` con `.test.ts(x)` | `usecases/__tests__/Get.test.ts` |
| Backend NestJS | `tests/` dentro del modulo con `.spec.ts` | `modules/debug/tests/debug.service.spec.ts` |

## Patron frontend

```typescript
describe('GetProductsUseCase', () => {
  let useCase: GetProductsUseCase;
  let mockRepo: jest.Mocked<IProductRepository>;

  beforeEach(() => {
    mockRepo = { findAll: jest.fn() } as any;
    useCase = new GetProductsUseCase(mockRepo);
  });

  it('should return products', async () => {
    mockRepo.findAll.mockResolvedValue([{ id: '1', name: 'P' }]);
    const result = await useCase.execute({});
    expect(result.products).toHaveLength(1);
  });

  it('should throw on invalid input', async () => {
    await expect(useCase.execute({ limit: -1 })).rejects.toThrow();
  });
});
```

## Patron backend (NestJS)

```typescript
describe('DebugService', () => {
  let service: DebugService;

  beforeEach(async () => {
    const module = await Test.createTestingModule({
      providers: [DebugService],
    }).compile();
    service = module.get(DebugService);
  });

  it('should return greeting', () => {
    expect(service.getGreeting()).toHaveProperty('message');
  });
});
```

## Validacion

```bash
npx jest --coverage
```

- Coverage < 80% → **ESCRIBIR MÁS TESTS**. No es detenerse, es CORREGIR.
- Test falla → corregir antes de continuar.
- NO hacer commit sin pasar este paso.
